# Data stores

Postgres through Prisma is the app database: users, verse sets, reviews, and sessions. New user data goes in Prisma via `@/prisma`.

MongoDB is only the Bible corpus. Look it up through `actions/fetchVerse.ts`. Do not add another route or client that queries the same collections.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — app data in Mongo, or a second Bible fetch
await mongoose.model('UserVerse').create({ userId, verseText });

// ✅ GOOD — app rows in Prisma, scripture text from the existing action
const verse = await fetchVerse(book, chapter, startingVerse, translation);
await prisma.userVerse.create({ data: { userId, verseText: verse.text } });
```
